\[ \text{Assessed Value} = \$18,400 \times 0.65 \]  
\[ \text{Assessed Value} = \$11,960 \]

### Step 2: Calculate the tax
The tax rate is \$4.57 per \$100 of the assessed value.  
First, determine how many \$100 units are in the assessed value:  
\[ \text{Number of \$100 units} = \frac{\text{Assessed Value}}{100} \]  
\[ \text{Number of \$100 units} = \frac{\$11,960}{100} = 119.6 \]  

Now, multiply the number of \$100 units by the tax rate:  
\[ \text{Tax} = \text{Number of \$100 units} \times \text{Tax Rate} \]  
\[ \text{Tax} = 119.6 \times \$4.57 \]  
\[ \text{Tax} = \$546.572 \]  

Rounding to the nearest cent, the tax is \$546.57.

### Step 3: Match the answer with the options
The correct answer is option 10: \$546.57.

